":"https:\/\/tyremap.com\/emission-zones\/bari\/"}</script><script type=application/ld+json>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"One with camera gates: the Città Vecchia. AMTAB, which issues the permits, defines it as the whole old town bounded by Corso Vittorio Emanuele, Piazza Massari, Piazza Isabella d'Aragona, Corso De Tullio, Lungomare Imperatore Augusto and Piazza IV Novembre."},"name":"How many ZTLs does Bari have?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No such procedure exists. Neither the Comune nor AMTAB provides for hotel or B\u0026B guests, so without one of the listed permits the gate records the plate. Park outside the old town and ask the accommodation where the nearest car park is."},"name":"Can my hotel or B\u0026B register my plate for Bari Vecchia?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The rules admit only light electric vehicles that count as bicycles, and only where signs allow it. An electric car without a permit is treated like any other car."},"name":"Are electric cars exempt in Bari?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Neither the Comune nor AMTAB publishes its own amount, so article 7 comma 14 of the Codice della Strada applies: EUR 83 to EUR 332, with 30% off if paid within five days. Repeat passes into the zone on the same day count as one violation."},"name":"What is the fine in Bari?"}]}</script><script type=application/ld+json>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://tyremap.com","name":"Home","position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://tyremap.com/emission-zones/","name":"Emission Zones","position":2},{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://tyremap.com/emission-zones/bari/","name":"Bari ZTL 2026: One Old-Town Zone, Seven Gates, No Guest Pass","position":3}]}</script><script type=applicati