xt-slate-300">TyreMap Emission-Zone Dataset</a> — 596 verified European emission zones, free to reuse under CC&nbsp;BY&nbsp;4.0.</p><section class=my-8><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=space-y-3><div class="faq-item border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 rounded-xl overflow-hidden"><button class="faq-toggle w-full flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 text-left bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-slate-700/70 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
<span class="font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 pr-4">How many ZTLs does Bari have?</span>
<svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0 text-slate-400 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentcolor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg></button><div class=faq-answer-wrap><div class=faq-answer-inner><p class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">One with camera gates: the Città Vecchia. AMTAB, which issues the permits, defines it as the whole old town bounded by Corso Vittorio Emanuele, Piazza Massari, Piazza Isabella d'Aragona, Corso De Tullio, Lungomare Imperatore Augusto and Piazza IV Novembre.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 rounded-xl overflow-hidden"><button class="faq-toggle w-full flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 text-left bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-slate-700/70 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
<span class="font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 pr-4">Can my hotel or B&amp;B register my plate for Bari Vecchia?</span>
<svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0 text-slate-400 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentcolor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg></button><div class=faq-answer-wrap><div class=faq-answer-inner><p class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">No such procedure exists. Neither the Comune nor AMTAB provides for hotel or B&amp;B guests, so without one of the listed permits the gate records the plate. Park outside the old town and ask the accommodation where the nearest car park is.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 rounded-xl overflow-hidden"><button class="faq-toggle w-full flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 text-left bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-slate-700/70 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
<span class="font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 pr-4">Are electric cars exempt in Bari?</span>
<svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0 text-slate-400 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentcolor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg></button><div class=faq-answer-wrap><div class=faq-answer-inner><p class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">No. The rules admit only light electric vehicles that count as bicycles, and only where signs allow it. An electric car without a permit is treated like any other car.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 rounded-xl overflow-hidden"><button class="faq-toggle w-full flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 text-left bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-slate-700/70 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
<span class="font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 pr-4">What is the fine in Bari?</span>
<svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0 text-slate-400 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentcolor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg></button><div class=faq-answer-wrap><div class=faq-answer-inner><p class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Neither the Comune nor AMTAB publishes its own amount, so article 7 comma 14 of the Codice della Strada applies: EUR 83 to EUR 332, with 30% off if paid within five days. Repeat passes into the zone on the same day count as one violation.</p></div></div></div></div></section><aside class="my-8 flex items-start gap-4 bg-white dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 rounded-2xl p-5" itemscope itemtype=https://schema.org/Person><a href=/authors/tyremap-editorial/ class=flex-shrink-0><img src=/images/authors/tyremap-team.svg alt="TyreMap Editorial Team" width=56 height=56 loading=lazy class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full" itemprop=image></a><div class=min-w-0><div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-x-2 mb-1"><a href=/authors/tyremap-editorial/ class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm hover:text-indigo-600 dark:hover:text-indigo-400" itemprop=name>TyreMap Editorial Team</a>
